From 9e70856eaf2a344801f20e1137ec341e9efeb0d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:03:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] US-10.3: the composite walk, one collection, and a carry
 limit

- CompositeIterator: stack of iterators, pre-order, remove() pops a removed box's children
- Room: chest field and getChest/setChest/hasChest gone; getChests(); contents() is the composite walk
- RoomPopulator puts the chest on the floor; RoomContentsIterator deleted
- TurnSnapshot records every container's contents in an IdentityHashMap (undo at any depth)
- Player.carriedWeight()/canCarry(); live carried weight on the status line
- TakeCommand refuses an over-capacity take before anything moves
- CommandParser: loot targets the top level; describeRoom lists chests and their children
- Chest.directCount(); repaired CommandTest/FactoryTest and the full IteratorCompositeTest

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019UKquNsPhGiV4vsiZoUekR
